@node Standard procedures
@nodedescription Built-in procedures.
@chapter Standard procedures
This chapter describes Scheme's built-in procedures.  The procedures
@nc{force}, @nc{promise?}, and @nc{make-promise} are intimately
associated with the expression types @nc{delay} and @nc{delay-force},
and are described with them in section 4.2.5 (@ref{Delayed evaluation}).
In the same way, the procedure @nc{make-parameter} is intimately
associated with the expression type @nc{parameterize}, and is described
with it in section 4.2.6 (@ref{Dynamic bindings}).

A program can use a global variable definition to bind any variable.  It
may subsequently alter any such binding by an @define{assignment}
(@pxref{Assignments}).  These operations do not modify the behavior of
any procedure defined in this report or imported from a library
(@pxref{Libraries}).  Altering any global binding that has not been
introduced by a definition has an unspecified effect on the behavior of
the procedures defined in this chapter.

@cindex fresh locations
@cindex conceptual locations @subentry freshness @seeentry{fresh locations}
@cindex newly allocated storage @subentry freshness @seeentry{fresh locations}
@cindex storage @subentry freshness @seeentry{fresh locations}
When a procedure is said to return a @define{newly allocated object}, it
means that the locations in the object are @emph{fresh}.
